## 3. Graph / Subgraph — Kahan Hai?

**Aap ka poora graph `backend/main.py` mein hai.** Yeh ek hi LangGraph state machine hai — koi alag subgraph nahi bana. (LangGraph mein subgraphs bante jab aap chhote graphs ko bare graph ke andar daalte; aap ke project mein aisa nahi hai.)

### Graph ka structure (flow):

```
START
  │
  ▼
PLANNER ──(topic ko 3-5 questions mein todta hai)──▶ RESEARCHER (PARALLEL)
  │                                                        │
  │            Har question ke liye 1 researcher chalta hai │
  │            (LangGraph ka "Send" mechanism)              │
  ▼                                                        ▼
                          VERIFIER (claims check)
  │                                                        │
  ▼                                                        ▼
                          DEDUP (duplicates hatao)
  │                                                        │
  ▼                                                        ▼
                          WRITER (briefing likho)
  │                                                        │
  ▼                                                        ▼
                          DELIVERER (approval + email)
  │                                                        │
  ▼                                                        ▼
                          END
```

### Key points:
- **Nodes** (steps): `planner`, `researcher`, `verifier`, `dedup`, `writer`, `deliverer`
- **Entry point**: `planner`
- **Parallel fan-out**: Planner ke baad, har sub-question ke liye **alag researcher node** parallel chalta hai (code mein `route_to_researchers` function yeh karta hai — har question ke liye ek `Send()` bhejta hai)
- **State**: Saara data `AgentState` (graph/state.py) mein rehta hai. `raw_findings` aur `errors` ka `operator.add` reducer hai — matlab parallel researchers ke results sab accumulate hote hain, ek doosre ko overwrite nahi karte
- **Human-in-the-loop**: `deliverer_node` mein `interrupt()` hai — yahan pipeline ruk jaati hai aur aap ki approval ka wait karti hai (approve / edit / reject)
- **Checkpointing**: Graph `SqliteSaver` ke saath compile hota hai jo state ko `db/checkpoints.sqlite` mein save karta hai. Agar app band ho jaye to bhi run ko wahan se resume kiya ja sakta hai

### `graph/supervisor.py` — naam theek hai kaam alag
Is file ka naam "supervisor" hai lekin **yeh koi supervisor agent nahi hai**. Yeh sirf ek chhota wrapper hai jo `main.py` se `build_app()` import kar ke graph return karta hai. Matlab naam se dhoka mat khana — asli kaam `main.py` mein hai.

