## 5. Agents (5 Agents — Har Ek Ka Kaam)

### `planner.py` — Planner Agent
- **Kyun bana**: Ek bare topic ko chhote research questions mein todne ke liye
- **Kaam**: `plan_research(topic)` — Ollama `llama3.2:3b` model se prompt bhejta hai ke 3-5 searchable questions ki JSON array banao. JSON parse hone par list return hoti hai, warna empty list
- **Detail**: Temperature 0 (deterministic output), markdown fences strip karta hai

### `researcher.py` — Researcher Agent
- **Kyun bana**: Web se asli claims collect karne ke liye
- **Kaam**: `research_question(question, max_results=3)` — `search_web()` se top 3 results lata hai, 100 chars se chhoti content skip karta hai, phir LLM se claim strings nikaalta hai
- **Khaas fix**: Source URL ko LLM ke bharose nahi chhorta — code mein programmatically asli search result ki URL attach karta hai (kyunki LLM hallucinated URLs deta tha — notes.md Failure #1)
- Output: `{claim, source_url, confidence: None, is_new: None}`

### `verifier.py` — Verifier Agent (sab se complex)
- **Kyun bana**: Hallucinations (jhoothe claims) rokne ke liye — yeh anti-hallucination layer hai
- **Kaam**: `verify_findings(findings)` — claims ko source URL ke hisaab se group karta hai aur har source ki pages dobara padhta hai (reader.py), phir batch mein verify karta hai
- **LLM selection**: `VERIFIER_PROVIDER` config ke mutabiq — `groq` (llama-3.3-70b-versatile) ya `ollama` (llama3.2:3b). Default ollama
- **Verdicts**: `confirmed` | `flagged` | `rejected` | `error`
  - Sirf `confirmed` ya `flagged` + confidence ≥ 0.5 wale pass hote hain
  - `error` verdict hamesha fail hote hain (fail-closed) — yeh sahi design hai
- **Batching**: Claims per-source group karke batch JSON mein verify kiye jate hain (LLM calls 4-5x kam). Agar batch JSON parse fail ho to per-claim fallback retry
- **Confidence check**: `MIN_CONFIDENCE = 0.5` — sirf verdict hi nahi, confidence score bhi check hota hai

### `writer.py` — Writer Agent
- **Kyun bana**: Final briefing report likhne ke liye
- **Kaam**: `write_briefing(topic, new_findings)` — findings ko 2 groups mein todta hai:
  - High confidence (≥0.7) → "confirmed facts" section
  - Low confidence (0.5-0.69) → "Unconfirmed / needs review" section
- Har claim ke saath "why it matters" note + source URL
- Findings empty hon to "No new developments" string

### `deliverer.py` — Deliverer Agent
- **Kyun bana**: Final briefing ko email karne ke liye
- **Kaam**: `send_briefing_email(subject, body)` — Gmail SMTP (`smtp.gmail.com:465`, SSL) ke through email bhejta hai. App password se login, default recipient khud (aap ki email)
- **Note**: `tools/email.py` file khali hai — asli email code YAHAN hai
- Iska graph node (deliverer_node) approval ke liye rukta hai, phir email bhejta hai

